{com}{err}Some control variables are not taken into account for groups with baseline treatment equal to: [0]
This may occur in the following situations:
1. For groups with those values of the baseline treatment, the regression of the outcome first difference on the controls' first differences and time fixed effects has fewer observations than variables. Note that for each value of the baseline treatment, those regressions are estimated among (g,t)s such that g has not changed treatment yet at t.
2. For groups with those values of the baseline treatment, two or more of your control variables are perfectly collinear in the sample where the regression is run, for instance because those control variables do not vary over time.
